{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Adding Rational Expressions.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Adding Rational Expressions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"adding rational expressions adding rational expressions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Adding Rational Expressions.md","fileName":"Adding Rational Expressions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Adding Rational Expressions","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial and Rational Expressions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Common Denominator","Like Terms","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Adding Rational Expressions.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Adding Rational Expressions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"adding rational expressions adding rational expressions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Adding Rational Expressions.md","fileName":"Adding Rational Expressions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Adding Rational Expressions","heading":"Adding Rational Expressions","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Adding or subtracting rational expressions requires a shared denominator, just as with numerical fractions. Factor the denominators, construct a [[Common Denominator]] containing the needed factors, rewrite each numerator, combine the numerators, and simplify if possible.\n\nFor denominators (x-3) and (x+2), the product ((x-3)(x+2)) is a common denominator unless factors are already shared. Domain restrictions from every original denominator remain in force. Expanding the combined numerator may expose [[Like Terms]], while factoring may expose later cancellation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Common Denominator","Like Terms","algebraessentials.pdf